WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.000
- Hey, babe, you ready to go?

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.640
- We can't go out there.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.950
- Why not?

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.390
- They're everywhere, invisible,

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.810
waiting for their next victim.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:09.940
It's not safe.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.700
- Julia, we talked about this.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.210
We're vaccinated, Austin's
only in stage three.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.490
As long as we mask up, it should be fine.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.600
- I'm not talking about COVID.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.186
- Then what?

00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:23.503
- Hidden fees.

00:00:23.503 --> 00:00:26.003
(jolly music)

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:36.059
- According to consumer
reports, between 2017 and 2019,

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:39.750
85% of Americans encountered hidden fees.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.530
Of these people, 96% found them annoying.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.870
That's right, 4% of people
are either super zen

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.390
or super rich.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.640
- Hidden fees are common
in many industries.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.180
You've likely seen them if
you've bought tickets online,

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.690
booked a hotel room,
bought a house or a car,

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.200
signed up for internet or cable,

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.260
or done anything with a bank.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.090
While you can opt out once
you see the real price,

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:05.380
many people don't have the
time or energy to do so.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.740
They either don't want to
go through the process again

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:08.870
with another seller,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.830
or they assume these
charges are inescapable.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.780
- This gradual reveal approach

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.960
is what economists called drip pricing.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.940
Sellers advertise a deceptively low price

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.750
to lure in customers.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.260
Then, once they're about to pay,

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:26.870
the hidden fees come out
and swarm their prey.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:30.410
- Why do so many companies
employ this shady practice?

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:34.070
Surely they don't want to offend
potential customers, right?

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.640
Well, whether or not they feel
morally conflicted about it,

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.190
from a business point of view,

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:40.360
they don't have much of a choice.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.330
This was demonstrated

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:44.520
in a 2015 experiment conducted by StubHub.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.210
- The experiment consisted
of showing one group

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:51.220
of shoppers their full ticket
price upfront, including fees.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.330
A second group only saw
the fees at the end,

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.020
when they were on the
verge of making a purchase.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.530
The results found that
people who saw the fees

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.780
at the end spent over 20% more

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.200
than those who received
the total price upfront.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.680
- In other words, hidden fees work.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.040
The only way for a seller
to stay competitive

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.750
is by hiding fees like everyone else,

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:16.520
otherwise their listed
price will seem much higher

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.630
than the competition,

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:20.250
even if the total costs
ends up being less.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.910
The current system practically
incentivizes hiding fees.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.420
To not do so is to lose money,

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.590
not just a little money either.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.090
Large banks pulled in $11.5 billion

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.470
in overdraft charges in 2018.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:37.610
The hotel industry made
nearly three billion in fees

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:38.890
during that same year,

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:41.970
which included fees for
amenities like pools and gyms,

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.270
whether you used those services or not.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:46.640
And the airline industry in 2018 earned

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.340
a combined $7.6 billion in baggage fees

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.430
and reservation change fees.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.380
The most frightening
part about all of this,

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:56.730
these numbers continue to go up.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.130
- Sadly, this is a problem

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.540
the market likely won't fix on its own,

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.410
which is why a petition is in place

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.510
to get drip pricing banned.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.050
The Federal Trade Commission
has been warning companies

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:08.820
to stop this practice for years,

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.460
but hasn't really done anything about it.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.620
Drip pricing has been banned
at the local level before,

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.300
but the only federal ban

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.410
was from the Department of Transportation,

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.230
aimed specifically at
the airline industry.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.420
- That doesn't mean we're doomed, though,

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.940
about 2/3 of people who fight
hidden fees are successful.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.860
Winning this battle is not guaranteed,

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.760
but if you're willing to get in the ring,

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.110
it's not impossible.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.900
So put on your gloves and
let's look at five ways

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.750
to defeat hidden fees.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.090
- The first way to destroy hidden fees

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.570
is to actually notice that they're there.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.900
A lot of hidden fees stay hidden,

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.890
which can easily happen
if you have auto-pay.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:50.050
You can protect yourself from
these thousand little cuts

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:52.760
by reviewing your statements periodically.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.610
If that sounds too overwhelming,

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:57.350
maybe choose a once a month review.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.000
- Now that you've spotted the fee,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.730
the second step is to just ask.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:02.600
That's right,

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.910
sometimes all it takes
is picking up the phone

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:05.880
or marching in there

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.140
and asking whether they'll waive the fee.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.510
You'd be surprised how often this works.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:12.210
Hotels are frequently willing

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:15.920
to remove the safe warranty
fee if you don't use the safe.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.420
You may be able to get car dealers

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.070
to remove the advertising fee,

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.490
which is the fee they charge
for marketing the car.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.640
Some people have even gotten home sellers

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.160
to cover some of the
closing costs themselves.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.290
It's worth a shot.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:29.220
- If you can't get a fee removed,

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.620
you can try finding a different seller.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.970
It may be frustrating to start
the purchase all over again,

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.110
but at least you'll know in the future

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.150
which sellers you can trust.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.970
- The fourth way to avoid
fees is to simply not use

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.230
the optional services.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.770
For example, if you're flying

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:46.760
and you don't want to pay the baggage fee,

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:50.420
you can just pack a smaller
bag that will fit on the plane.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:53.140
- And the fifth and
final way to escape fees

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:57.110
is by seeing if the seller has
some sort of loyalty program.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.790
Some hotels, for example,

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:02.120
will waive fees if you sign
up for their credit card.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:04.010
Yes, there is some risk involved,

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:06.270
especially if you lack self-control,

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:07.830
but if you're disciplined enough,

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.700
you can earn rewards and get fees waived.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:11.900
Pretty cool deal.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:12.860
- If you're like us,

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.470
you're in the 96% of people

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:17.000
who find hidden fees
annoying and deceptive.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.850
While there are ways around them,

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.680
they're not always avoidable.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:24.210
And until the FTC steps in,
we're kind of stuck with them.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:26.210
- But if you really wanna fight them,

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:29.660
you could support ethical
sellers, write a review online,

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:32.810
file a complaint, or
send a letter to the FTC.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:37.326
Together, we can defeat these
pesky beasts once and for all.

00:05:37.326 --> 00:05:39.080
And that's our two cents.
- And that's our two cents.

